          material: 'A supplied sheet from the same made-up project. It permits text-secondary on surface-raised, but the contrast table from lesson 4 has no row for that pair: it measured text-secondary on surface-base only.',
          question: 'What should happen to that pairing?',
          options: [
            { label: 'Measure it now; until it is measured it is not permitted.', correct: true, feedback: 'An unmeasured pairing is an assumption that the raised surface is close enough to the base. That is exactly the sort of drift a sheet exists to prevent.' },
            { label: 'Allow it, since text-secondary passed on the base surface.', feedback: 'A raised surface is a different colour. Passing on one background says nothing about another.' },
            { label: 'Prohibit it, because it was not measured.', feedback: 'Prohibiting without measuring throws away a pairing that may be perfectly good. Measure first, then decide.' },
            { label: 'Allow it with a note that it is unverified.', feedback: 'A permitted-with-doubt pairing will be used as permitted. The note will not travel with it.' },
          ],
          then: 'Go through your own permitted list and measure anything your contrast table does not already cover.',
