          beats: [
            { label: 'What I did first', text: 'I clicked through the paper screens and timed myself. About two seconds a screen, no waiting anywhere. I wrote down that the flow felt quick.' },
            { label: 'Why that was empty', text: 'Nothing in a paper flow can be slow. I had measured my own hand moving cards, not a product.' },
            { label: 'What I changed', text: 'My sister held the paper screen face down and counted four seconds on her phone before turning it over. That was the whole apparatus.' },
            { label: 'What appeared', text: 'I pressed the button twice during the second wait, and said out loud “did that work?”. On paper I had never once pressed anything twice.' },
            { label: 'What I wrote down', text: 'Four seconds, paper screens, a person counting, one person watching. Labelled a rehearsal. It gave me a problem worth testing properly, not a finding.' },
          ],
          wrongTurn: 'The wrong turn is reporting the counted wait as a test of loading. Nobody waited for a real page; a person turned a card over.',
          tradeoff: 'The rehearsal costs you any right to speak about real timings. What you get is a problem you did not know existed, for the price of four seconds and a phone.',
